# Line endings are a BUILD dependency here, not a style preference.
#
# `prebuild` runs `check:design`, which parses fenced ```css blocks out of
# docs/TOKENS.md with a regex requiring "```css\n". With core.autocrlf=true —
# the default on Windows — a fresh clone checks that file out as CRLF, every
# fence stops matching, and the build fails with "Type has no ```css block" on
# all five token sections at once. That happened on 2026-08-13 from nothing more
# than a `git stash` / `stash pop` round trip.
#
# Vercel is unaffected (Linux checkout, LF), which is exactly what makes this
# the dangerous kind of bug: it only ever breaks a developer machine, and it
# breaks it at prebuild rather than anywhere near the change that caused it.
#
# `text=auto eol=lf` normalises to LF in the repo AND in the working tree, so
# the guard's assumption holds on every platform.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary — never touch these.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.avif binary
*.mp4 binary
*.pdf binary
